Notebook[{Cell["Transversely polarized proton-proton classes (A_TT), step 2 \
(FeynCalc route): spin and colour algebra", "Title"], 
  Cell["Input: the amplitudes of step 1 for the class chosen below.  Output: \
Results/FeynCalc/class-<n>/Algebra.wl with\n  Born:       the Born square for \
the two transverse spin projections defined below (TT and Symmetric), summed \
over final spins and colours, averaged over the initial colours, in D \
dimensions;\n  Virtual:    the interference 2 Re(M_1loop M_Born^ for the same \
projections, written in terms of scalar one-loop integrals (families \
VirtualST, VirtualSU, VirtualTU as in Processes/Hadronic) with D-dimensional \
coefficients;\n  Real:       the weighted sum over the real-emission \
processes of the class of |M|^2 for the same projections, with the unobserved \
momenta k1, k2 explicit (step 3 integrates them);\n  BornTable:  the \
D-dimensional transversely polarized Born squares |M|^2/gs^4 of every 2 -> 2 \
channel needed by the collinear counterterms of the five classes (q qb -> q' \
qb', q q -> q q, q qb -> q qb, q qb -> g g, with their a <-> b relabellings), \
in the format of Processes/PartonicBorn, checked against the lowest-order \
cross sections of Soffer, Stratmann and Vogelsang \
(reference/SSV-born.wl).\nThe squaring method, the colour treatment, the \
gluon polarization sums, the scalar-integral families and the parallel \
organization are those of Processes/Hadronic/2-Algebra-FeynCalc.wl (read that \
file first); only the spin projections of the two incoming partons \
differ.\n\nSpin densities (docs/TRANSVERSE-PP.md).  Both incoming partons are \
quarks or antiquarks with a transverse spin: u ubar -> pa-slash gamma5 \
sa-slash/2 and v vbar -> the same expression (for a massless antiquark v(p,s) \
vbar(p,s) = p-slash (1 + gamma5 s-slash)/2 as for the quark); these are the \
densities whose partonic cross section multiplies the transversity \
distribution delta f = f(up,up) - f(down,up) of each proton, i.e. the \
partonic quantity computed here is (1/2)[sigma(up,up) - sigma(up,down)].  The \
spin vectors are four-dimensional, orthogonal to pa and pb, and are written \
in the basis of the scattering plane of pa, pb, p: the in-plane axis eX, \
along the transverse momentum of the observed parton,\n\n   eX = Sqrt[s/(t \
u)] [ p + (u/s) pa + (t/s) pb ],   eX.pa = eX.pb = 0,  eX^2 = -1,  eX.p = \
-Sqrt[t u/s] = -pT,\n\nand the normal n ~ eps^{mu pa pb p}, n^2 = -1, n.pa = \
n.pb = n.p = 0, so that sa = cos(phia) eX + sin(phia) n and sb = cos(phib) eX \
+ sin(phib) n.  The squared matrix element is then T = XX cos(phia) cos(phib) \
+ NN sin(phia) sin(phib) + XN cos(phia) sin(phib) + NX sin(phia) cos(phib), \
and the four components are computed separately (XX from the unnormalized \
axis aX = p + (u/s) pa + (t/s) pb, aX^2 = -t u/s, divided by -aX^2; XN and NX \
up to the positive factor Sqrt[s/(t u)]).  Parity (reflection through the \
scattering plane) demands XN = NX = 0: for the real emission these components \
are odd in the normal component of the unobserved momentum and vanish after \
the phase-space integration.\n\nThe observable.  With both proton spins along \
one direction x and the observed parton at azimuth Phi with respect to it, T \
= (XX+NN)/2 + (XX-NN)/2 cos(2 Phi).  The physical cross section has no \
Phi-independent part (the two helicity flips carry two units of angular \
momentum along the beam: XX + NN = 0 in four dimensions, which is checked \
below), and the hard part of A_TT is the coefficient of cos(2 Phi),\n\n   \
delta sigma_TT = (XX - NN)/2   (\"TT\"),   which equals the projection with \
F(p, sa, sb) = (s/(t u)) [2 (p.sa)(p.sb) + (t u/s) sa.sb] of Mukherjee, \
Stratmann and Vogelsang (F = +1 for sa = sb = eX, -1 for sa = sb = n).\n\nIn \
the HVBM scheme the symmetric part (XX + NN)/2 (\"Symmetric\") does not \
vanish in D dimensions: the two hatted gamma matrices that connect the two \
densities give a term proportional to (D - 4) s^2 (sa.sb) at Born level, and \
hatted momenta give similar terms at NLO.  This evanescent, Phi-independent \
part is kept as a separate projection through step 4 (where its poles must \
still cancel) and never enters TT, which is why TT is defined as the \
antisymmetric combination and not as XX alone.\n\nNormal components.  n.k1 = \
-n.k2 = nr appears in NN, XN and NX of the real emission; its odd powers \
integrate to zero and nr^2 is a rational function of the invariants: with k1 \
= k1par + c n + k1hat (parts in the plane of pa, pb, p, along n, and in the \
D-4 extra dimensions), n.k1 = -c, and k1^2 = 0 gives nr^2 = k1par^2 + spe3, \
k1par^2 = d.G^-1.d with G the Gram matrix of pa, pb, p and d = (pa.k1, pb.k1, \
p.k1) (Processes/Collins, normalReduction).  The loop momentum has a normal \
component too: the decomposition is the same, (n.loop)^2 = looppar^2 - loop^2 \
+ loopHat2, with looppar^2 written through the propagators, and the odd \
powers vanish because the tensor loop integrals are built from pa, pb, p \
only; aX.loop is a combination of pa.loop, pb.loop, p.loop.\n\nInvariants as \
in Processes/Hadronic: s = (pa+pb)^2, t = (pa-p)^2, u = (pb-p)^2; real \
emission: s4 = (k1+k2)^2 = s + t + u, A = (pa-k1)^2, B = (pb-k1)^2, C = \
(p+k1)^2 with A + B + C = -s4; spe3 = k1hat.k1hat.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load", "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Choices: the class; the number of parallel kernels for the squares \
(\"auto\" = one per processor core, at most 8; \"1\" = none); and whether the \
product files of an earlier run of this same, unchanged file may be reused \
(\"no\" recomputes everything; \"yes\" only continues an interrupted run: a \
product file is reused only if its companion file <name>.input holds the \
fingerprint of the current inputs, the amplitudes of step 1 and this step \
file; a file written for other inputs, or without that companion (for \
example, after an interrupted write), is computed again).", "Text"], 
  Cell["LoadFeynCalc[];\n(* FeynCalc expresses this memoization threshold in \
MB; transient algebra can use more memory. *)\nFeynCalc`$FCMemoryAvailable = \
Min[FeynCalc`$FCMemoryAvailable, Floor[1024^3/10^6]];\nclass = \
\"5\";\nworkers = \"auto\";\nresume = \"no\";\nloaded = \
LoadAmplitudes[\"class-\" <> class];\namplitudes = loaded[\"FeynCalc\"]; spec \
= loaded[\"Spec\"]; weights = loaded[\"Weights\"];\nspec", "Input"], 
  Cell["Conventions", "Section"], Cell["The conventions, the kinematics and \
the spin axes are installed by functions, because every parallel kernel \
installs them too.  The axes aX and nn are vectors of their own whose scalar \
products with every momentum are set from the definitions above (defineAxes), \
as in Processes/Collins; nn.k1 = nr and nn.k2 = -nr in the real kinematics, \
nn.k1 = 0 in the Born kinematics (k1 = pa + pb - p), and nn.loop stays \
symbolic until the virtual section reduces it.  One unobserved momentum is \
not independent: inside the amplitudes k2 is replaced by pa + pb - p - k1 \
(real emission) and k1 by pa + pb - p (Born and one loop), except in the \
external spinors, whose spin sums give the slashed momentum itself.", 
   "Text"], Cell["conventions := (FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"]; \
$LeviCivitaSign = -1);\nconventions;\naxisCoefficients = {u/s, t/s, 1};       \
               (* aX = (u/s) pa + (t/s) pb + p *)\ndefineAxes[momenta_List, \
normalComponents_List] := Module[{base = {pa, pb, p}, ca = \
axisCoefficients},\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {aX, nn}];\n  \
Do[SP[aX, x] = SPD[aX, x] = Factor[Sum[ca[[i]] SP[base[[i]], x], {i, 3}]], \
{x, momenta}];\n  SP[aX] = SPD[aX] = Factor[Sum[ca[[i]] ca[[j]] SP[base[[i]], \
base[[j]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\n  SP[nn] = SPD[nn] = -1; SP[aX, nn] = SPD[aX, \
nn] = 0;\n  Scan[(SP[nn, #] = SPD[nn, #] = 0) &, {pa, pb, p}];\n  Do[SP[nn, \
rule[[1]]] = SPD[nn, rule[[1]]] = rule[[2]], {rule, \
normalComponents}]];\nbornKinematics := (FCClearScalarProducts[]; \
SetMandelstam[s, t, u, pa, pb, -p, -k1, 0, 0, 0, 0];\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D - \
4] = 0) &, {pa, pb, p, k1}];\n  defineAxes[{pa, pb, p, k1}, {k1 -> \
0}]);\nrealKinematics := (FCClearScalarProducts[];\n  SPD[pa] = 0; SPD[pb] = \
0; SPD[p] = 0; SPD[k1] = 0; SPD[k2] = 0;\n  SPD[pa, pb] = s/2; SPD[pa, p] = \
-t/2; SPD[pb, p] = -u/2;\n  SPD[pa, k1] = -A/2; SPD[pb, k1] = -B/2; SPD[p, \
k1] = C/2;\n  SPD[pa, k2] = (s + t + A)/2; SPD[pb, k2] = (s + u + B)/2; \
SPD[p, k2] = (-t - u - C)/2; SPD[k1, k2] = (s + t + u)/2;\n  \
Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {pa, pb, p}];\n  (* hatted parts of the \
unobserved momenta, and their four-dimensional products (SP = SPD - SPE; the \
physical momenta have no hatted parts) *)\n  Pair[Momentum[k1, D - 4], \
Momentum[k1, D - 4]] = spe3; Pair[Momentum[k2, D - 4], Momentum[k2, D - 4]] = \
spe3;\n  Pair[Momentum[k1, D - 4], Momentum[k2, D - 4]] = -spe3;\n  SP[k1] = \
-spe3; SP[k2] = -spe3; SP[k1, k2] = (s + t + u)/2 + spe3;\n  SP[pa] = 0; \
SP[pb] = 0; SP[p] = 0; SP[pa, pb] = s/2; SP[pa, p] = -t/2; SP[pb, p] = \
-u/2;\n  SP[pa, k1] = -A/2; SP[pb, k1] = -B/2; SP[p, k1] = C/2;\n  SP[pa, k2] \
= (s + t + A)/2; SP[pb, k2] = (s + u + B)/2; SP[p, k2] = (-t - u - C)/2;\n  \
defineAxes[{pa, pb, p, k1, k2}, {k1 -> nr, k2 -> -nr}]);\nbornConservation = \
k1 -> pa + pb - p;\nrealConservation = k2 -> pa + pb - p - k1;\nincoming = \
spec[\"Born\"] /. None -> spec[\"Real\"][[1, 1]];       (* the two incoming \
partons *)\nincoming = incoming[[1 ;; 2]];\nRequire[FreeQ[incoming, \"g\"], \
\"The transversely polarized process needs two incoming quarks or \
antiquarks\", incoming];\n(* the spin axes of pa and pb for each component, \
and the normalization that turns the axis aX into the unit vector eX (XN, NX: \
up to Sqrt[s/(t u)]) *)\ncomponents = {\"XX\", \"NN\", \"XN\", \
\"NX\"};\nspinAxes = <|\"XX\" -> <|pa -> aX, pb -> aX|>, \"NN\" -> <|pa -> \
nn, pb -> nn|>, \"XN\" -> <|pa -> aX, pb -> nn|>, \"NX\" -> <|pa -> nn, pb -> \
aX|>|>;\nnormalization[spinCase_] := If[spinCase === \"XX\", s/(t u), \
1];\naverage[spinCase_] := 1/(2 Nc)^2;                                   (* \
1/(2 Nc) per incoming quark: the 1/2 of the density (1 +- gamma5 s-slash)/2 \
and the colour average *)\ncolourFactors[expr_] := Factor[expr /. SUNN -> Nc] \
/. (-1 + Nc) (1 + Nc) -> 2 Nc CF /. Nc -> \
CA;\nbornKinematics;\nRequire[Simplify[{SP[aX, pa], SP[aX, pb], SP[aX] + t \
u/s, SP[aX, p] + t u/s, SP[aX, k1] - t u/s, SP[nn, aX], SP[nn] + 1} /. u -> \
-s - t] === {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},\n  \"The in-plane axis is not what the \
text says\"];\n{incoming, average[\"XX\"], SP[aX]}", "Input"], 
  Cell["The squaring method", "Section"], Cell["As in Processes/Hadronic: (1) \
every amplitude is simplified once (Lorentz contraction, Dirac algebra on the \
open chains, one independent unobserved momentum, transversality eps(l).l = \
eps(l).r = 0 of every gluon with its reference vector r); (2) colour is \
separated and each colour network evaluated once; (3) only the products i <= \
j are formed; (4) the gluon polarization sums are applied one gluon at a time \
on grouped tensors; (5) the products are distributed over parallel kernels, \
one file per product.  The only change is in the fermion spin sums (step 4 of \
the method): after FermionSpinSum, the slashed momenta of the two incoming \
partons are replaced by the densities pa-slash gamma5 sa-slash and pb-slash \
gamma5 sb-slash with the axes of the component being computed (the factor 1/2 \
of each density is in average).", "Text"], Cell["(* ---- 1. one amplitude \
---- *)\ngluonsOf[expr_] := Union[Cases[expr, Polarization[l_, __] :> l, \
Infinity]];\ntransversality[references_] := Flatten[Table[{\n    \
Pair[Momentum[Polarization[l, ___], ___], Momentum[l, ___]] -> 0,\n    \
Pair[Momentum[Polarization[l, ___], ___], Momentum[references[l], ___]] -> \
0}, {l, Keys[references]}]];\n(* eps(x).x = 0 for the eliminated momentum x = \
sum_q c_q q: solve it for eps(x).q of the last momentum q that is not x's \
reference vector *)\neliminatedTransversality[rule_, references_] := \
Module[{x = rule[[1]], terms = termList[Expand[rule[[2]]]], momenta, \
coefficient, solved},\n  momenta = Cases[terms, c_. q_Symbol :> q];\n  solved \
= Last[DeleteCases[momenta, references[x]]];\n  coefficient[q_] := \
Coefficient[rule[[2]], q];\n  Pair[Momentum[Polarization[x, h___], d1___], \
Momentum[solved, d2___]] :>\n    -Sum[coefficient[q] \
Pair[Momentum[Polarization[x, h], d1], Momentum[q, d2]], {q, \
DeleteCases[momenta, solved]}]/coefficient[solved]];\n(* momentum \
conservation inside propagators and vertices, not in the external spinors \
(Spinor[...] is matched first and left unchanged) *)\nconserve[expr_, rule_] \
:= expr /. {sp_Spinor :> sp, Momentum[q_, dim___] /; FreeQ[q, Polarization] \
&& !FreeQ[q, rule[[1]]] :>\n  Momentum[Expand[q /. rule], \
dim]};\nprepare[amp_, references_, rule_] := Module[{a = conserve[amp, \
rule]},\n  a = FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit[a];\n  a = \
DiracSimplify[Contract[a]];\n  a = ExpandScalarProduct[a] /. \
eliminatedTransversality[rule, references] /. transversality[references];\n  \
Expand[a]];\n\n(* ---- 2. colour ---- *)\ncolourHead = SUNTF | SUNT | SUNF | \
SUNDelta | SUNFDelta | SUNTrace;\nfactorList[term_] := If[Head[term] === \
Times, List @@ term, {term}];\ntermList[expr_] := If[Head[expr] === Plus, \
List @@ expr, {expr}];\ncolourPart[term_] := Times @@ \
Select[factorList[term], !FreeQ[#, SUNIndex | SUNFIndex] &];\n(* {{c_x, L_x}, \
...}: the distinct colour structures of an amplitude with their Lorentz parts \
*)\ncolourGroups[amp_] := Module[{groups = GatherBy[termList[Expand[amp]], \
colourPart]},\n  Table[{colourPart[First[g]], Total[(#/colourPart[#]) & /@ \
g]}, {g, groups}]];\ncolourCache = <||>;\ncolourValue[network_] := \
Module[{key = FCCanonicalizeDummyIndices[network, Head -> {SUNIndex, \
SUNFIndex}, FCI -> True,\n    SUNIndexNames -> Table[Symbol[\"cA\" <> \
ToString[k]], {k, 30}], SUNFIndexNames -> Table[Symbol[\"cF\" <> \
ToString[k]], {k, 30}]], value},\n  If[KeyExistsQ[colourCache, key], \
Return[colourCache[key]]];\n  value = SUNSimplify[key /. SUNF[a_, b_, c_] :> \
-2 I (SUNTrace[SUNT[a] . SUNT[b] . SUNT[c]] - SUNTrace[SUNT[b] . SUNT[a] . \
SUNT[c]]),\n    Explicit -> True, SUNTraceEvaluate -> True, SUNNToCACF -> \
False];\n  value = Factor[value /. SUNN -> Nc];\n  If[!FreeQ[value, \
colourHead | SUNIndex | SUNFIndex], Return[Failure[\"Colour\", <|\"Network\" \
-> key, \"Value\" -> value|>]]];\n  colourCache[key] = value];\n\n(* ---- 4. \
spin sums and gluon polarization sums ---- *)\npolarizationSum[l_, mu_, nu_, \
r_] := -MTD[mu, nu] + (FVD[l, mu] FVD[r, nu] + FVD[r, mu] FVD[l, nu])/SPD[l, \
r];\ntag[l_] := Symbol[ToString[l] <> \"Spin\"];\nindexNames[l_] := \
{Symbol[\"mu\" <> ToString[l]], Symbol[\"nu\" <> \
ToString[l]]};\ntensorPart[term_, {mu_, nu_}] := Times @@ \
Select[factorList[term], !FreeQ[#, LorentzIndex[mu | nu, ___]] &];\n(* the \
contraction uses the installed scalar products, which differ between the Born \
and the real kinematics: the kinematics are part of the key *)\n(* Each \
worker reuses identical contractions across diagram pairs. The explicit\n   \
spin projections and the original BMHV trace evaluation are unchanged. \
*)\ncurrentKinematics = None;\nalgebraCacheScope[] := {\"HadronicTT\", class, \
currentKinematics, \"BMHV\", $LeviCivitaSign};\ninitializeAlgebraCaches[] := \
(\n  traceAlgebraCache = CreateBoundedAlgebraCache[\n    Function[structure, \
Contract[DiracSimplify[structure, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True]]], 32768, 128 \
2^20];\n  tensorAlgebraCache = CreateBoundedAlgebraCache[\n    \
Function[product, ExpandScalarProduct[Contract[Expand[product]]]], 8192, 128 \
2^20]);\ninitializeAlgebraCaches[];\ncanonicalTraceStructure[structure_] := \
FCCanonicalizeDummyIndices[structure,\n  FCI -> True, Head -> {LorentzIndex}, \
DotSimplify -> False, FCTraceExpand -> False,\n  LorentzIndexNames -> \
Table[Symbol[\"algebraDummy\" <> ToString[j]], {j, \
40}]];\ngroupedTrace[expr_] := Module[{rows, groups},\n  (* Pure-gluon terms \
have no trace to evaluate; leave their scalar sums sparse. *)\n  \
If[FreeQ[expr, _DiracTrace | _DiracGamma | _DOT], Return[expr]];\n  rows = \
GroupIdenticalAlgebraTerms[expr, _DiracTrace | _DiracGamma | _LorentzIndex | \
_Eps | _DOT];\n  If[FailureQ[rows], Return[rows]];\n  rows = \
{canonicalTraceStructure[#[\"Structure\"]], #[\"Coefficient\"]} & /@ rows;\n  \
groups = GatherBy[rows, First];\n  Total[Table[With[{structure = \
First[First[group]], coefficient = Together[Total[Last /@ group]]},\n    \
If[coefficient === 0, 0,\n      coefficient \
traceAlgebraCache[\"Apply\"][{algebraCacheScope[], structure}, structure]]], \
{group, groups}]]];\nprojectOnce[tensor_, density_] := \
tensorAlgebraCache[\"Apply\"][\n  {algebraCacheScope[], tensor, density}, \
tensor density];\nproject[expr_, l_, density_] := Module[{idx = \
indexNames[l], groups},\n  groups = GroupIdenticalAlgebraTerms[expr, \
LorentzIndex[idx[[1]] | idx[[2]], ___]];\n  If[FailureQ[groups], \
Return[groups]];\n  Total[(#[\"Coefficient\"] projectOnce[#[\"Structure\"], \
density]) & /@ groups]];\n(* the colour-weighted product of the Lorentz parts \
of one pair: spin sums with the transverse densities of pa and pb, traces, \
polarization sums\n   (every external gluon of these classes is outgoing) \
*)\nspinSum[product_, spinCase_, references_, gluonList_] := Module[{expr = \
product, axes = spinAxes[spinCase]},\n  expr = expr /. (With[{l = #, lTag = \
tag[#]}, Spinor[c_. Momentum[l, D], m_, o_] :> Spinor[c Momentum[lTag, D], m, \
o]] & /@ {pa, pb});\n  expr = expr /. Flatten[Table[{Momentum[Polarization[l, \
I, ___], D] -> LorentzIndex[indexNames[l][[1]], D],\n    \
Momentum[Polarization[l, -I, ___], D] -> LorentzIndex[indexNames[l][[2]], \
D]}, {l, gluonList}]];\n  expr = FermionSpinSum[expr];\n  expr = expr /. \
(With[{l = #, lTag = tag[#], ax = axes[#]}, DiracGamma[Momentum[lTag, D], D] \
:> GSD[l] . GA[5] . GS[ax]] & /@ {pa, pb});\n  If[!FreeQ[expr, tag[pa] | \
tag[pb]], Return[Failure[\"Density\", <|\"Message\" -> \"a tagged spinor \
momentum survived the density insertion\"|>]]];\n  (* Contract the same gluon \
polarization sums while their Lorentz indices\n     are still carried by \
compact traces; avoid a large expanded tensor. *)\n  Do[expr = project[expr, \
l, polarizationSum[l, Sequence @@ indexNames[l], references[l]]], {l, \
gluonList}];\n  expr = groupedTrace[expr];\n  If[!FreeQ[expr, _Failure], \
Return[FirstCase[expr, _Failure, Failure[\"Trace\", <||>], Infinity]]];\n  \
ExpandScalarProduct[Contract[expr]]];\n\n(* ---- 3. one product (i, j) of \
colour-separated amplitudes: left = {{c_x, L_x}, ...}, right = {{c_y^*, \
L_y^*}, ...} ---- *)\ninterference[left_, right_, spinCase_, references_] := \
Module[{product},\n  product = Total[Flatten[Table[colourValue[x[[1]] y[[1]]] \
x[[2]] y[[2]], {x, left}, {y, right}]]];\n  If[!FreeQ[product, Failure], \
FirstCase[product, _Failure, Null, Infinity],\n    spinSum[product, spinCase, \
references, gluonsOf[{left, right}]]]];\nconjugateGroups[amp_] := \
colourGroups[ComplexConjugate[amp, FCRenameDummyIndices -> True]];\n(* the \
real part: after expanding, every term is a number times real symbols (the \
denominators are real propagators), so the real part of the number is kept \
*)\nrealPartOf[expr_] := Expand[expr] /. Complex[a_, b_] :> a;\n\n(* ---- the \
normal component of an unobserved or loop momentum x: polynomial in nx = n.x; \
odd powers integrate to zero, nx^2 = xpar^2 - x4.x4\n   with xpar^2 = \
d.G^-1.d (d the products of x with pa, pb, p; G their Gram matrix) and x4.x4 \
the four-dimensional square of x ---- *)\ngramMatrix[products_] := \
Table[products[x, y], {x, {pa, pb, p}}, {y, {pa, pb, \
p}}];\nparallelSquare[d_List, gram_] := Factor[d . Inverse[gram] . \
d];\nnormalReduction[expr_, nx_, parallel_, fourSquare_] := \
Module[{coefficients = CoefficientList[Expand[expr], nx]},\n  If[coefficients \
=== {}, coefficients = {0}];                                   (* a vanishing \
expression (a graph can vanish exactly) *)\n  Require[Length[coefficients] <= \
3, \"A power of the normal component above two appeared\", \
Length[coefficients] - 1];\n  <|\"Even\" -> coefficients[[1]] + \
If[Length[coefficients] == 3, coefficients[[3]] (parallel - fourSquare), \
0],\n    \"Odd\" -> If[Length[coefficients] >= 2, coefficients[[2]], \
0]|>];\n\"squaring functions defined\"", "Input"], 
  Cell["Parallel kernels: each loads FeynFacet and FeynCalc, installs the \
conventions and receives the functions above; each job installs its \
kinematics (Born or real).  Every job (one product of the squaring method, \
one spin component) is written to Results/FeynCalc/class-<n>/pairs/<name>.wl \
with its time.  A diagonal product |M_i|^2 is real; its epsilon-tensor terms \
may leave an imaginary part that vanishes only after simplification, which is \
checked to be exactly zero at a rational point and dropped.", "Text"], 
  Cell["feynFacetFile = FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \
\"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}];\nnWorkers = If[workers === \"auto\", \
Min[$ProcessorCount, 8], ToExpression[workers]];   (* \"auto\": one per \
processor core, at most 8 *)\nIf[nWorkers > 1,\n  LaunchKernels[nWorkers];\n  \
With[{file = feynFacetFile}, ParallelEvaluate[Get[file]; LoadFeynCalc[];\n    \
FeynCalc`$FCMemoryAvailable = Min[FeynCalc`$FCMemoryAvailable, \
Floor[1024^3/10^6]]]];\n  DistributeDefinitions[conventions, \
axisCoefficients, defineAxes, bornKinematics, realKinematics, gluonsOf, \
transversality, eliminatedTransversality, conserve, prepare,\n    colourHead, \
factorList, termList, colourPart, colourGroups, colourValue, polarizationSum, \
tag, indexNames, tensorPart,\n    projectOnce, project, spinSum, \
interference, conjugateGroups, realPartOf, spinAxes,\n    algebraCacheScope, \
initializeAlgebraCaches, canonicalTraceStructure, groupedTrace];\n  \
ParallelEvaluate[conventions; colourCache = <||>; currentKinematics = None; \
initializeAlgebraCaches[]]];\npairDirectory = \
FileNameJoin[{ResultsDirectory[\"FeynCalc/class-\" <> class], \
\"pairs\"}];\nIf[!DirectoryQ[pairDirectory], \
CreateDirectory[pairDirectory]];\n(* the fingerprint of the inputs of the \
product files: the amplitudes of step 1 and this step file (see the choice \
resume above) *)\ninputFingerprint = InputFingerprint[loaded, {\n  \
FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"2-Algebra-FeynCalc.wl\"}],\n  \
FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"AlgebraReuse.wl\"}]}];\nrunJob[job_] := Module[{file = \
FileNameJoin[{pairDirectory, job[\"Name\"] <> \".wl\"}], value, seconds},\n  \
If[resume === \"yes\" && ReusableQ[file, inputFingerprint], file,\n    (* \
Algebra caches remain local to this worker and bounded across pairs. *)\n    \
If[job[\"Kinematics\"] === \"Born\", bornKinematics, realKinematics]; \
currentKinematics = job[\"Kinematics\"];\n    {seconds, value} = \
AbsoluteTiming[interference[job[\"Left\"], job[\"Right\"], job[\"Spin\"], \
job[\"References\"]]];\n    If[!FreeQ[value, Failure], value,\n      \
Put[<|\"Name\" -> job[\"Name\"], \"Value\" -> value, \"Seconds\" -> \
seconds|>, file]; MarkReusable[file, inputFingerprint]]]];\nrunJobs[jobs_] := \
Module[{files},\n  DistributeDefinitions[runJob, pairDirectory, resume, \
inputFingerprint];\n  files = If[nWorkers > 1, ParallelMap[runJob, jobs, \
Method -> \"FinestGrained\"], Map[runJob, jobs]];\n  Require[FreeQ[files, \
Failure], \"A job failed\", FirstCase[files, _Failure, Null, Infinity]];\n  \
Get /@ files];\n(* the pairs i <= j of a square, and their sum: diagonal \
products as they are, i < j twice the real part *)\nsquareJobs[name_, sides_, \
kinematics_, references_, spinCase_] := Flatten[Table[\n  <|\"Name\" -> name \
<> \"-\" <> spinCase <> \"-\" <> ToString[i] <> \"-\" <> ToString[j], \
\"Kinematics\" -> kinematics,\n    \"Left\" -> sides[[1, i]], \"Right\" -> \
sides[[2, j]], \"Spin\" -> spinCase, \"References\" -> references, \"Pair\" \
-> {i, j}|>,\n  {i, Length[sides[[1]]]}, {j, i, \
Length[sides[[1]]]}]];\ncheckPoint = {s -> 1, t -> -3/10, u -> -2/5, A -> \
-1/7, B -> -2/9, C -> -3/10 + 1/7 + 2/9, D -> 37/10, Nc -> 3, spe3 -> 1/11, \
nr -> 3/13, gs -> 1, Nf -> 5};\nimaginaryPartOf[expr_] := (expr - (expr /. \
Complex[a_, b_] :> Complex[a, -b]))/2;\nsquare[name_, sides_, kinematics_, \
references_, spinCase_] := Module[{jobs = squareJobs[name, sides, kinematics, \
references, spinCase], results},\n  results = runJobs[jobs];\n  Require[And \
@@ MapThread[#2[\"Pair\"][[1]] != #2[\"Pair\"][[2]] || \
(imaginaryPartOf[#1[\"Value\"]] /. checkPoint) === 0 &, {results, jobs}],\n   \
 \"A diagonal product has a nonzero imaginary part\", name];\n  \
Total[MapThread[If[#2[\"Pair\"][[1]] == #2[\"Pair\"][[2]], \
realPartOf[#1[\"Value\"]], 2 realPartOf[#1[\"Value\"]]] &, {results, \
jobs}]]];\nsidesOf[amps_, references_, rule_] := With[{prepared = prepare[#, \
references, rule] & /@ amps}, {colourGroups /@ prepared, conjugateGroups /@ \
prepared}];\n\"parallel kernels: \" <> ToString[Max[1, Length[Kernels[]]]]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Born", "Section"], Cell["The Born square with the \
reference vectors p -> pa, k1 -> pa for the gluons, for the four components; \
then the checks XN = NX = 0 (exactly) and XX + NN = 0 in four dimensions, and \
the two projections TT = (XX - NN)/2 and Symmetric = (XX + NN)/2.  The \
evanescent symmetric part is displayed.", "Text"], 
  Cell["bornReferences = <|pa -> pb, pb -> pa, p -> pa, k1 -> \
pa|>;\nbornKinematics;\nbornSides = If[amplitudes[\"Born\"] === {}, None, \
sidesOf[amplitudes[\"Born\"], bornReferences, \
bornConservation]];\nbornComponents = If[bornSides === None, Association[# -> \
0 & /@ components],\n  Association @ Table[sc -> With[{sq = square[\"born\", \
bornSides, \"Born\", bornReferences, sc]},\n    bornKinematics; \
Factor[colourFactors[Together[average[sc] normalization[sc] sq]] /. u -> -s - \
t]], {sc, components}]];\nRequire[FreeQ[bornComponents, Complex | Pair | \
Momentum | LorentzIndex | Eps], \"The Born square is not a real scalar\", \
bornComponents];\nRequire[bornComponents[\"XN\"] === 0 && \
bornComponents[\"NX\"] === 0, \"The mixed components of the Born square do \
not vanish\", bornComponents];\nRequire[Factor[(bornComponents[\"XX\"] + \
bornComponents[\"NN\"]) /. D -> 4] === 0, \"XX + NN of the Born square does \
not vanish in four dimensions\", bornComponents];\nborn = <|\"TT\" -> \
Factor[(bornComponents[\"XX\"] - bornComponents[\"NN\"])/2], \"Symmetric\" -> \
Factor[(bornComponents[\"XX\"] + bornComponents[\"NN\"])/2],\n  \"XX\" -> \
bornComponents[\"XX\"], \"NN\" -> bornComponents[\"NN\"]|>;\nborn", "Input"], 
  Cell["The transversely polarized Born table", "Section"], 
  Cell["The D-dimensional Born squares |M|^2/gs^4 (colours and spins of the \
unobserved parton summed, colours of a and b averaged, the two transverse \
densities inserted) of every 2 -> 2 channel a b -> c that the collinear \
counterterms of the five classes need: q qb -> q' (and qb'), q q -> q, q qb \
-> q (and qb), q qb -> g, their a <-> b relabellings (qb q -> ...), and the \
charge conjugate qb qb -> qb; plus the control channels q q' -> q, q q' -> \
q', q qb' -> q, which must vanish (classes 1-4: the two polarized partons on \
different fermion lines).  They are computed directly, as in \
Processes/Collins/6-ResolvedBorn.wl (FeynCalc's generic spin sum with the \
densities inserted, the polarization sums with reference vector pa, \
SUNSimplify for the colour), independently of the parallel squaring machinery \
above, and the class's own Born square must agree with its table entry.  Keys \
as in Processes/PartonicBorn (\"q qb -> qp\"); each entry holds XX, NN, TT \
and Symmetric.\n\nChecks: XN = NX = 0 and XX + NN = 0 in four dimensions for \
every channel; the a <-> b relabelled channel equals the original with t <-> \
u (the axis aX is symmetric, the normal changes sign for both densities); the \
charge conjugate equals its representative; the control channels vanish; and \
at D = 4, Nc = 3 the TT entries reproduce Table I of Soffer, Stratmann and \
Vogelsang: with sigma = s E dsigma/d^3p = 2 s^2 dsigma/(dt du dPhi) and \
dsigma/(dt du dPhi) = dsigma/(dt dPhi) delta(s4), the cos(2 Phi) coefficient \
of their Eq. (6) corresponds to |M|^2_TT/gs^4 = (4/9) (t u/s^2) delta|M|^2 \
(the hard part is alphaS^2 |M|^2_TT/(gs^4 s v) delta(1-w), \
Processes/Hadronic/4-Unpolarized.wl).", "Text"], 
  Cell["tableKinematics := (FCClearScalarProducts[]; SetMandelstam[s, t, u, \
pa, pb, -p, -pd, 0, 0, 0, 0];\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {pa, pb, p, \
pd}]; defineAxes[{pa, pb, p, pd}, {pd -> 0}]);\ntableChannels = {{\"q\", \
\"qb\", \"qp\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"qpb\"}, {\"q\", \"q\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \
\"qb\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"qb\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"g\"},\n  {\"qb\", \
\"q\", \"qp\"}, {\"qb\", \"q\", \"qpb\"}, {\"qb\", \"q\", \"q\"}, {\"qb\", \
\"q\", \"qb\"}, {\"qb\", \"q\", \"g\"}, {\"qb\", \"qb\", \
\"qb\"}};\ncontrolChannels = {{\"q\", \"qp\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qp\", \
\"qp\"}, {\"q\", \"qpb\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qpb\", \"qpb\"}};\nfield = \
<|\"q\" -> F[3, {1}], \"qb\" -> -F[3, {1}], \"qp\" -> F[3, {2}], \"qpb\" -> \
-F[3, {2}], \"g\" -> V[5]|>;\nchannelName[{a_, b_, c_}] := a <> \" \" <> b <> \
\" -> \" <> c;\nflavourNumber[x_] := Switch[x, \"q\", {1, 0}, \"qb\", {-1, \
0}, \"qp\", {0, 1}, \"qpb\", {0, -1}, \"g\", {0, 0}];\npartner[{a_, b_, c_}] \
:= Module[{ok = Select[Keys[field], Total[flavourNumber /@ {a, b}] === \
Total[flavourNumber /@ {c, #}] &]},\n  Require[Length[ok] == 1, \"The \
unobserved parton of \" <> channelName[{a, b, c}] <> \" is not unique\", ok]; \
First[ok]];\ntableDiagrams[ch_] := InsertFields[CreateTopologies[0, 2 -> 2], \
{field[ch[[1]]], field[ch[[2]]]} -> {field[ch[[3]]], field[partner[ch]]},\n  \
InsertionLevel -> {Classes}, Model -> \"SMQCD\", ExcludeParticles -> {S[_], \
U[_], V[1 | 2 | 3], F[1 | 2 | 4], F[3, {3}]}];\ntableAmplitude[ch_] := \
Total[FCFAConvert[CreateFeynAmp[tableDiagrams[ch], Truncated -> False, \
PreFactor -> 1],\n  IncomingMomenta -> {pa, pb}, OutgoingMomenta -> {p, pd}, \
UndoChiralSplittings -> True, ChangeDimension -> D,\n  List -> True, SMP -> \
False, Contract -> False, DropSumOver -> True,\n  FinalSubstitutions -> \
{FCGV[\"MU\"] -> 0, FCGV[\"MC\"] -> 0}] /. SMP[\"g_s\"] -> gs /. GaugeXi[_] \
-> 1];\ntableReferences = <|p -> pa, pd -> pa|>;\ntableSquare[amp_, \
spinCase_] := Module[{conj, expr, gluons, indices, axes = \
spinAxes[spinCase]},\n  tableKinematics;\n  gluons = Union[Cases[amp, \
Polarization[l_, __] :> l, Infinity]];\n  indices = Association @ \
Table[gluons[[i]] -> {Symbol[\"mu\" <> ToString[i]], Symbol[\"nu\" <> \
ToString[i]]}, {i, Length[gluons]}];\n  expr = amp ComplexConjugate[amp];\n  \
expr = expr /. (With[{l = #, lTag = tag[#]}, Spinor[c_. Momentum[l, D], m_, \
o_] :> Spinor[c Momentum[lTag, D], m, o]] & /@ {pa, pb});\n  expr = expr /. \
Flatten[Table[{Momentum[Polarization[l, I, ___], D] -> \
LorentzIndex[indices[l][[1]], D],\n    Momentum[Polarization[l, -I, ___], D] \
-> LorentzIndex[indices[l][[2]], D]}, {l, gluons}]];\n  expr = expr Times @@ \
Table[polarizationSum[l, indices[l][[1]], indices[l][[2]], \
tableReferences[l]], {l, gluons}];\n  expr = \
FermionSpinSum[FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit[expr]];\n  expr = expr /. (With[{l \
= #, lTag = tag[#], ax = axes[#]}, DiracGamma[Momentum[lTag, D], D] :> GSD[l] \
. GA[5] . GS[ax]] & /@ {pa, pb});\n  Require[FreeQ[expr, tag[pa] | tag[pb]], \
\"A tagged spinor momentum survived the density insertion (table)\"];\n  expr \
= DiracSimplify[expr, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] // Contract;\n  expr = \
SUNSimplify[expr, Explicit -> True, SUNNToCACF -> False] // Contract // \
ExpandScalarProduct;\n  Factor[colourFactors[Together[average[spinCase] \
normalization[spinCase] expr/gs^4 /. u -> -s - t]]]];\ntableEntry[ch_] := \
Module[{amp = tableAmplitude[ch], xx, nnv, xn, nx},\n  {xx, nnv, xn, nx} = \
tableSquare[amp, #] & /@ components;\n  Require[FreeQ[{xx, nnv, xn, nx}, \
Complex | Pair | Momentum | LorentzIndex | Eps | SUNIndex], \"A table entry \
is not a real scalar\", channelName[ch]];\n  Require[xn === 0 && nx === 0, \
\"The mixed components of a table entry do not vanish\", {channelName[ch], \
xn, nx}];\n  Require[Factor[(xx + nnv) /. D -> 4] === 0, \"XX + NN of a table \
entry does not vanish in four dimensions\", {channelName[ch], xx, nnv}];\n  \
<|\"XX\" -> xx, \"NN\" -> nnv, \"TT\" -> Factor[(xx - nnv)/2], \"Symmetric\" \
-> Factor[(xx + nnv)/2]|>];\ntableEntries = Association @ \
Table[channelName[ch] -> tableEntry[ch], {ch, Join[tableChannels, \
controlChannels]}];\nbornTable = Association @ Table[key -> Map[#[key] &, \
tableEntries], {key, {\"TT\", \"Symmetric\", \"XX\", \
\"NN\"}}];\nTableForm[Normal[Map[Simplify[# /. D -> 4] &, \
bornTable[\"TT\"]]]]", "Input"], Cell["tableCheck[expr_] := Factor[expr /. u \
-> -s - t];\nRequire[And @@ \
Table[tableCheck[bornTable[\"TT\"][channelName[ch]]] === 0 && \
tableCheck[bornTable[\"Symmetric\"][channelName[ch]]] === 0, {ch, \
controlChannels}],\n  \"A control channel of the Born table does not \
vanish\", Map[bornTable[\"TT\"], channelName /@ controlChannels]];\n(* a <-> \
b: pa <-> pb exchanges t and u, i.e. t -> -s - t in the entries (u is \
eliminated) *)\nswapped[name_] := Module[{parts = StringSplit[name, \" \"]}, \
parts[[2]] <> \" \" <> parts[[1]] <> \" -> \" <> \
parts[[4]]];\nrelabelDifferences = Association @ Flatten[Table[{key, name} -> \
tableCheck[bornTable[key][swapped[name]] - (bornTable[key][name] /. t -> -s - \
t)],\n    {key, {\"TT\", \"Symmetric\"}}, {name, channelName /@ \
Select[tableChannels, #[[1]] === \"q\" && #[[2]] === \"qb\" \
&]}]];\nRequire[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ Values[relabelDifferences]), \"An a <-> \
b relabelled entry is not the t <-> u image of the original\", \
Select[relabelDifferences, # =!= 0 \
&]];\nRequire[tableCheck[bornTable[\"TT\"][\"qb qb -> qb\"] - \
bornTable[\"TT\"][\"q q -> q\"]] === 0 && \
tableCheck[bornTable[\"Symmetric\"][\"qb qb -> qb\"] - \
bornTable[\"Symmetric\"][\"q q -> q\"]] === 0,\n  \"The charge-conjugate \
channel differs from its representative\"];\n(* the class's own Born square \
(the parallel machinery) against the table (the direct computation) \
*)\nIf[spec[\"Born\"] =!= None,\n  Require[And @@ \
Table[tableCheck[born[key]/gs^4 - \
bornTable[key][StringRiffle[spec[\"Born\"][[1 ;; 2]], \" \"] <> \" -> \" <> \
spec[\"Born\"][[3]]]] === 0, {key, {\"TT\", \"Symmetric\", \"XX\", \
\"NN\"}}],\n    \"The Born square of the class differs from its table \
entry\", born]];\n(* the literature: Table I of Soffer, Stratmann and \
Vogelsang at D = 4, Nc = 3 *)\nGet[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"reference\", \"SSV-born.wl\"}]];\nliteratureDifferences = Association @ \
Table[name -> Factor[(bornTable[\"TT\"][name] /. {D -> 4, CA -> 3, CF -> 4/3} \
/. u -> -s - t) - ((4/9) (t u/s^2) SSVMatrixElement[name] /. u -> -s - t)],\n \
 {name, Keys[SSVMatrixElement]}];\nRequire[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ \
Values[literatureDifferences]), \"A transversely polarized Born square \
differs from Soffer, Stratmann and Vogelsang\", \
literatureDifferences];\n\"Born table checked: control channels vanish, a <-> \
b relabelling, charge conjugation, the class Born, and the literature at D = \
4, Nc = 3\"", "Input"], 
  Cell["Virtual: the one-loop interference in terms of scalar integrals", 
   "Section"], Cell["As in Processes/Hadronic: the loop propagators of every \
graph are mapped by a shift of the loop momentum onto one of the families \
VirtualST, VirtualSU, VirtualTU, the graph is contracted with the conjugate \
Born amplitude and the spin sums above, and the scalar products of the loop \
momentum are written through the inverse propagators Dj.  New here: the \
products aX.loop and nn.loop of the spin axes with the loop momentum.  \
aX.loop is the combination (u/s) pa.loop + (t/s) pb.loop + p.loop; nn.loop is \
reduced as explained in the introduction, (nn.loop)^2 = looppar^2 - loop^2 + \
loopHat2 with looppar^2 = d.G^-1.d, d = (loop.pa, loop.pb, loop.p), and its \
odd powers dropped (they integrate to zero).  The hatted loop.loop is kept as \
loopHat2 (HatPower[n]), shifting the dimension of the integral in step 3.", 
   "Text"], Cell["families = <|\n  \"VirtualST\" -> {loop, loop + pa, loop + \
pa + pb, loop + p},                 (* legs pa, pb, -pd, -p in cyclic order: \
invariants s and t *)\n  \"VirtualSU\" -> {loop, loop + pa, loop + pa + pb, \
loop + pa + pb - p},       (* legs pa, pb, -p, -pd: s and u *)\n  \
\"VirtualTU\" -> {loop, loop + pa, loop + pa - p, loop + pa - p + pb}|>;      \
(* legs pa, -p, pb, -pd: t and u *)\nfamilyHeads = <|\"VirtualST\" -> \
KVirtualST, \"VirtualSU\" -> KVirtualSU, \"VirtualTU\" -> \
KVirtualTU|>;\nshifts = Flatten[Table[c1 pa + c2 pb + c3 p, {c1, -1, 1}, {c2, \
-1, 1}, {c3, -1, 1}]];\npropagatorMomenta[amp_] := Union[Cases[amp, \
PropagatorDenominator[Momentum[q_, ___], 0] /; !FreeQ[q, loop] :> Expand[q /. \
bornConservation], Infinity]];   (* the loop propagators; tree propagators \
stay as they are *)\nsameUpToSign[q1_, q2_] := Expand[q1 - q2] === 0 || \
Expand[q1 + q2] === 0;\n(* find sigma, delta and the family such that every \
propagator of the graph, with loop -> sigma loop + delta, is one of the \
family's *)\nrouting[amp_] := Module[{props = propagatorMomenta[amp], \
found},\n  found = Catch[Do[If[And @@ Table[Or @@ Table[sameUpToSign[q /. \
loop -> sigma loop + delta, f], {f, families[name]}], {q, props}],\n      \
Throw[{name, sigma, delta}]], {name, Keys[families]}, {sigma, {1, -1}}, \
{delta, shifts}]; None];\n  Require[found =!= None, \"No family fits the \
propagators of a one-loop graph\", props]; found];\nroutings = routing /@ \
amplitudes[\"Virtual\"];\nCounts[routings[[All, 1]]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["loopProducts = {L2 -> Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[loop, D]], Lpa \
-> Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[pa, D]],\n  Lpb -> Pair[Momentum[loop, \
D], Momentum[pb, D]], Lp -> Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[p, D]]};       \
(* the four scalar products of the loop momentum (FeynCalc's internal form of \
SPD) *)\ninverseProps[name_] := Module[{q = families[name], dj, sol},\n  dj = \
Array[Dj, 4];\n  sol = Solve[Table[dj[[j]] == ExpandScalarProduct[SPD[q[[j]], \
q[[j]]]] /. Reverse /@ loopProducts, {j, 4}] /. u -> -s - t, {L2, Lpa, Lpb, \
Lp}];\n  Require[Length[sol] == 1, \"Cannot express the loop scalar products \
through the propagators\"]; First[sol]];\nloopRules[name_] := loopRules[name] \
= With[{sol = inverseProps[name]}, Table[(x /. loopProducts) -> (x /. sol), \
{x, {L2, Lpa, Lpb, Lp}}]];\n(* the shifted graph with its loop propagators as \
inert symbols DjOf[q] *)\nshiftedGraph[amp_, {name_, sigma_, delta_}] := \
Module[{shifted},\n  shifted = amp /. Momentum[q_, dim_] /; !FreeQ[q, loop] \
:> Momentum[Expand[q /. loop -> sigma loop + delta], dim] /.\n    \
PropagatorDenominator[c_. Momentum[q_, dim_], 0] :> \
PropagatorDenominator[Momentum[Expand[c q /. bornConservation], dim], 0];    \
(* c: FeynCalc writes Momentum[-loop] as -Momentum[loop] *)\n  shifted /. \
FeynAmpDenominator[ds__] :> Times @@ (Replace[#, {PropagatorDenominator[c_. \
Momentum[q_, ___], 0] /; FreeQ[q, loop] :> 1/ExpandScalarProduct[SPD[q, \
q]],\n    PropagatorDenominator[c_. Momentum[q_, ___], 0] :> 1/DjOf[c q]}] & \
/@ {ds})];\n(* the products of the spin axes with the loop momentum \
*)\naxisLoopRules = {\n  Pair[Momentum[aX, ___], Momentum[loop, ___]] :> \
axisCoefficients . {Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[pa, D]], \
Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[pb, D]], Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[p, \
D]]},\n  Pair[Momentum[loop, ___], Momentum[aX, ___]] :> axisCoefficients . \
{Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[pa, D]], Pair[Momentum[loop, D], \
Momentum[pb, D]], Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[p, D]]},\n  \
Pair[Momentum[nn, ___], Momentum[loop, ___]] -> nLoop, Pair[Momentum[loop, \
___], Momentum[nn, ___]] -> nLoop};\nloopParallelSquare := \
parallelSquare[{Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[pa, D]], Pair[Momentum[loop, \
D], Momentum[pb, D]], Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[p, D]]}, \
gramMatrix[SP]];\n(* the contracted interference of one graph -> sum of \
coefficient x family[indices] x HatPower[n]; the odd part in nn.loop is \
returned separately (it must vanish for XN, NX and is dropped) \
*)\ntoFamilies[expr0_, name_] := Module[{expr, fourDimensionalProducts, \
reduced},\n  (* the four-dimensional products of the HVBM scheme equal the \
D-dimensional ones for the four-dimensional external momenta, and loop4.loop4 \
= loop.loop - loophat.loophat *)\n  fourDimensionalProducts = \
{Pair[Momentum[loop], Momentum[loop]] -> Pair[Momentum[loop, D], \
Momentum[loop, D]] - loopHat2,\n    Pair[Momentum[loop], Momentum[x_]] /; \
FreeQ[x, aX | nn] :> Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[x, D]], \
Pair[Momentum[x_], Momentum[loop]] /; FreeQ[x, aX | nn] :> Pair[Momentum[x, \
D], Momentum[loop, D]]};\n  (* the spin sum of an outgoing quark k1 gives \
k1-slash: loop.k1 by momentum conservation *)\n  expr = \
ExpandScalarProduct[expr0] /. axisLoopRules /. fourDimensionalProducts /. \
Pair[Momentum[k1, D], Momentum[loop, D]] -> ExpandScalarProduct[SPD[pa + pb - \
p, loop]] /.\n    Pair[Momentum[loop, D - 4], Momentum[loop, D - 4]] -> \
loopHat2;\n  reduced = normalReduction[expr, nLoop, loopParallelSquare, \
Pair[Momentum[loop, D], Momentum[loop, D]] - loopHat2];\n  expr = \
reduced[\"Even\"] /. loopRules[name];\n  Require[FreeQ[expr, Momentum[loop, \
___]], \"A scalar product of the loop momentum was not expressed through the \
propagators\", Short[Union[Cases[expr, h_[a___] /; !FreeQ[{a}, Momentum[loop, \
___]] && FreeQ[h, Times | Plus | Power], Infinity]], 8]];\n  expr = \
Expand[expr /. DjOf[q_] :> Dj @@ (Position[families[name], f_ /; \
sameUpToSign[f, q]][[1]])];\n  (* every term is a coefficient times powers of \
the Dj (negative for propagators, positive for numerators) and of loopHat2 \
*)\n  <|\"Even\" -> Total[Table[With[{powers = Table[Exponent[term, Dj[j]], \
{j, 4}], hat = Exponent[term, loopHat2]},\n      (term/(Times @@ \
Table[Dj[j]^powers[[j]], {j, 4}] loopHat2^hat)) familyHeads[name] @@ \
(-powers) HatPower[hat]], {term, DeleteCases[termList[expr], 0]}]],   (* a \
graph can vanish exactly once eps(l).l = eps(l).r = 0 are imposed *)\n    \
\"OddLeafCount\" -> \
LeafCount[reduced[\"Odd\"]]|>];\nbornKinematics;\nvirtualLeft = \
MapThread[colourGroups[prepare[shiftedGraph[#1, #2], bornReferences, \
bornConservation]] &, {amplitudes[\"Virtual\"], routings}];\nbornSumRight = \
If[bornSides === None, {}, conjugateGroups[Total[prepare[#, bornReferences, \
bornConservation] & /@ amplitudes[\"Born\"]]]];\nLength[virtualLeft]", 
   "Input"], Cell["The interference 2 Re(M1 M0 with the measure conventions \
of Processes/Hadronic: FeynArts writes the one-loop amplitude with d^D \
loop/(2 Pi)^D, the scalar integrals are defined with d^D loop/(i Pi^(D/2)), \
and the association virtual holds Sum_j [i c_j M0*] I_j per component, with \
the hat powers as HatPower[n]; the factor 2/(4 Pi)^(D/2) is included in step \
4.  Checks: XN and NX vanish (their even parts in nn.loop; the odd parts, \
which integrate to zero, are dropped), and XX + NN vanishes in four \
dimensions once the hatted terms (which integrate to order eps) are dropped."\
, "Text"], Cell["virtualJobs[spinCase_] := Table[<|\"Name\" -> \"virtual-\" \
<> spinCase <> \"-\" <> ToString[g], \"Kinematics\" -> \"Born\", \"Left\" -> \
virtualLeft[[g]],\n  \"Right\" -> bornSumRight, \"Spin\" -> spinCase, \
\"References\" -> bornReferences|>, {g, \
Length[virtualLeft]}];\nvirtualComponents = If[amplitudes[\"Virtual\"] === \
{}, Association[# -> 0 & /@ components],\n  Association @ Table[spinCase -> \
Module[{results = runJobs[virtualJobs[spinCase]], graphs},\n    \
bornKinematics;\n    graphs = MapThread[toFamilies[#1[\"Value\"], #2[[1]]] &, \
{results, routings}];\n    oddLeafCounts[spinCase] = \
Total[#[\"OddLeafCount\"] & /@ graphs];\n    Collect[I average[spinCase] \
normalization[spinCase] Total[#[\"Even\"] & /@ graphs] /. u -> -s - t,\n      \
{_KVirtualST, _KVirtualSU, _KVirtualTU, _HatPower}, colourFactors]], \
{spinCase, components}]];\nRequire[FreeQ[virtualComponents, Complex | Eps | \
nLoop], \"The virtual interference is not real or still contains nn.loop\", \
Short[virtualComponents, 5]];\nRequire[virtualComponents[\"XN\"] === 0 && \
virtualComponents[\"NX\"] === 0, \"The mixed components of the virtual \
interference do not vanish\", {virtualComponents[\"XN\"], \
virtualComponents[\"NX\"]}];\nRequire[Collect[(virtualComponents[\"XX\"] + \
virtualComponents[\"NN\"]) /. HatPower[n_ /; n > 0] -> 0 /. HatPower[0] -> 1 \
/. D -> 4, {_KVirtualST, _KVirtualSU, _KVirtualTU}, Factor] === 0,\n  \"XX + \
NN of the virtual interference does not vanish in four \
dimensions\"];\nvirtual = <|\"TT\" -> Collect[(virtualComponents[\"XX\"] - \
virtualComponents[\"NN\"])/2, {_KVirtualST, _KVirtualSU, _KVirtualTU, \
_HatPower}, Factor],\n  \"Symmetric\" -> Collect[(virtualComponents[\"XX\"] + \
virtualComponents[\"NN\"])/2, {_KVirtualST, _KVirtualSU, _KVirtualTU, \
_HatPower}, Factor]|>;\n{Length[virtual[\"TT\"]], Union[Cases[virtual, \
(KVirtualST | KVirtualSU | KVirtualTU)[__], Infinity]] // Length, \
Map[Union[Cases[#, _HatPower, Infinity]] &, virtual],\n  \"leaf count of the \
dropped odd parts in nn.loop\" -> (oddLeafCounts /@ components)}", "Input"], 
  Cell["Real emission", "Section"], Cell["For every real-emission process of \
the class, the square of the sum of its diagrams for the four components, in \
terms of the invariants s, t, u, A, B, C, the hatted invariant spe3 and the \
normal component nr; the processes are added with their weights (classes.wl). \
 Reference vectors of the physical polarization sums: pa for the gluons p and \
k1, pb for k2.  Then the normal reduction: the parts odd in nr are dropped \
(they integrate to zero), nr^2 is replaced by k1par^2 + spe3.  Checks: the \
even parts of XN and NX vanish, and XX + NN vanishes in four dimensions \
without the hatted terms; both are evaluated exactly at random rational \
points of all invariants (the expressions have tens of thousands of terms).", 
   "Text"], Cell["realReferences = <|pa -> pb, pb -> pa, p -> pa, k1 -> pa, \
k2 -> pb|>;\nrealKinematics;\nrealSides = Association @ KeyValueMap[#1 -> \
sidesOf[#2, realReferences, realConservation] &, \
amplitudes[\"Real\"]];\nrealSquares = Association @ Table[spinCase -> \
Association @ KeyValueMap[\n    #1 -> square[\"real-\" <> StringReplace[#1, \
\" \" -> \"_\"], #2, \"Real\", realReferences, spinCase] &, realSides], \
{spinCase, components}];\nrealKinematics;\nrealParallelSquare = \
parallelSquare[{SP[pa, k1], SP[pb, k1], SP[p, k1]}, gramMatrix[SP]];      (* \
k1par^2 = d.G^-1.d *)\nrealReduced = Association @ Table[spinCase -> \
Association @ KeyValueMap[\n    #1 -> normalReduction[#2, nr, \
realParallelSquare, SP[k1]] &, realSquares[spinCase]], {spinCase, \
components}];       (* SP[k1] = -spe3: nr^2 = k1par^2 + spe3 *)\n(* the \
weighted sums per component (not brought to a common denominator: step 3 \
expands into partial fractions anyway); the colour factors are polynomials in \
Nc = CA *)\nrealComponents = Association @ Table[spinCase -> \
(average[spinCase] normalization[spinCase] Total[KeyValueMap[weights[#1] \
#2[\"Even\"] &, realReduced[spinCase]]] /. Nc -> CA), {spinCase, \
components}];\nRequire[FreeQ[realComponents, Complex | nr | nn | aX | Eps], \
\"The real-emission square is not real or still contains the normal \
component\"];\nRequire[FreeQ[realComponents, Pair | Momentum | LorentzIndex], \
\"A scalar product was left unevaluated in the real-emission square\", \
Union[Cases[realComponents, _Pair, Infinity]]];\n{realParallelSquare, \
Map[LeafCount, realComponents]}", "Input"], Cell["(* exact rational points of \
all invariants (C = -s4 - A - B), D, Nc, spe3 *)\nrealPoints = Table[With[{r \
= RandomInteger[{1, 97}, 8]/RandomInteger[{98, 197}, 8]},\n  {s -> 1, t -> \
-r[[1]], u -> -r[[2]] (1 - r[[1]]), A -> -r[[3]], B -> -r[[4]], D -> 4 - \
r[[5]], CA -> 2 + 10 r[[6]], CF -> 1 + r[[7]], spe3 -> r[[8]], Nf -> 5}], \
{3}];\natPoint[expr_, point_] := expr /. C -> -(s + t + u) - A - B /. \
point;\nRequire[And @@ Table[atPoint[realComponents[\"XN\"], point] === 0 && \
atPoint[realComponents[\"NX\"], point] === 0, {point, realPoints}],\n  \"The \
even parts of the mixed components of the real emission do not \
vanish\"];\nRequire[And @@ Table[atPoint[(realComponents[\"XX\"] + \
realComponents[\"NN\"]) /. {D -> 4, spe3 -> 0}, point] === 0, {point, \
realPoints}],\n  \"XX + NN of the real emission does not vanish in four \
dimensions\"];\nreal = <|\"TT\" -> (realComponents[\"XX\"] - \
realComponents[\"NN\"])/2, \"Symmetric\" -> (realComponents[\"XX\"] + \
realComponents[\"NN\"])/2|>;\nRequire[Max[Exponent[#, spe3] & /@ \
termList[Expand[real[\"TT\"] + real[\"Symmetric\"]]]] <= 1, \"The \
real-emission square has spe3^2 terms (step 3 has the masters in D + 2 \
only)\"];\n{\"odd parts dropped (leaf counts)\" -> \
Map[Total[KeyValueMap[LeafCount[#2[\"Odd\"]] &, #]] &, realReduced], \
LeafCount /@ real}", "Input"], Cell["Check of the gauge invariance of the \
real-emission square: for the first process of the class and the XX component \
(the one without normal components), the physical polarization sums with \
other reference vectors (pb for p and k1, pa for k2) give the same result.  \
The amplitudes are prepared again, since the conditions eps(l).r = 0 depend \
on the reference vectors.", "Text"], Cell["alternativeReferences = <|pa -> \
pb, pb -> pa, p -> pb, k1 -> pb, k2 -> pa|>;\nfirstProcess = \
First[Keys[amplitudes[\"Real\"]]];\nrealKinematics;\nalternative = \
square[\"gauge-\" <> StringReplace[firstProcess, \" \" -> \"_\"],\n  \
sidesOf[amplitudes[\"Real\"][firstProcess], alternativeReferences, \
realConservation], \"Real\", alternativeReferences, \"XX\"];\n(* the \
difference is evaluated exactly at random rational points (all invariants, D \
and Nc), with C = -s4 - A - B *)\ngaugePoints = Table[With[{v = \
RandomInteger[{1, 97}, 7]/RandomInteger[{98, 197}, 7]},\n  {s -> 1, t -> \
-v[[1]], u -> -v[[2]] (1 - v[[1]]), A -> -v[[3]], B -> -v[[4]], D -> 4 - \
v[[5]], Nc -> 2 + 10 v[[6]], spe3 -> v[[7]]}], {3}];\nreferenceDifference = \
Table[(alternative - realSquares[\"XX\"][firstProcess]) /. C -> -(s + t + u) \
- A - B /. point, {point, gaugePoints}];\nRequire[referenceDifference === {0, \
0, 0}, \"The real-emission square depends on the gluon reference vectors\", \
referenceDifference];\n\"gauge invariance of the real emission checked\"", 
   "Input"], Cell["Timing and save", "Section"], 
  Cell["The number of products computed, their total time and the longest \
one, in seconds (read from the product files).", "Text"], 
  Cell["pairTimes = Association @ Table[FileBaseName[f] -> \
Get[f][\"Seconds\"], {f, FileNames[\"*.wl\", \
pairDirectory]}];\nworkerReuseStatistics = If[nWorkers > 1,\n  \
ParallelEvaluate[<|\"Trace\" -> traceAlgebraCache[\"Statistics\"][],\n    \
\"Polarization\" -> tensorAlgebraCache[\"Statistics\"][], \"MemoryBytes\" -> \
MemoryInUse[]|>],\n  {<|\"Trace\" -> traceAlgebraCache[\"Statistics\"][],\n   \
 \"Polarization\" -> tensorAlgebraCache[\"Statistics\"][], \"MemoryBytes\" -> \
MemoryInUse[]|>}];\nSaveResult[\"AlgebraReuseMetrics\", <|\"Workers\" -> \
workerReuseStatistics,\n  \"PairJobs\" -> Length[pairTimes], \
\"TotalWorkerSeconds\" -> Total[pairTimes]|>, \"FeynCalc/class-\" <> \
class];\n{Length[pairTimes], Round[Total[pairTimes]], Round[Max[pairTimes]]}"\
, "Input"], Cell["Save the Born square, the virtual interference, the \
real-emission square (projections TT and Symmetric) and the Born table for \
steps 3 and 4, and close the parallel kernels.", "Text"], 
  Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \"Virtual\" -> virtual, \"Real\" -> \
real, \"BornTable\" -> bornTable, \"Class\" -> class, \"Spec\" -> spec,\n  \
\"Families\" -> families, \"Projections\" -> \"TT = (XX - NN)/2 (the cos(2 \
Phi) coefficient, the hard part of A_TT); Symmetric = (XX + NN)/2 (evanescent \
in the HVBM scheme)\",\n  \"Variables\" -> \"s, t, u = -s-t; A = (pa-k1)^2, B \
= (pb-k1)^2, C = (p+k1)^2 = -s4-A-B; spe3; loopHat2 via HatPower[n]; Born \
table: |M|^2/gs^4 in s, t, D, CF, CA\"|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \
\"FeynCalc/class-\" <> class];\nCloseKernels[];\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
